    <description>AppGeek scans what is already installed on the machine, shows what has an update waiting, and
updates the lot in one run. It is a proper front end for winget rather than a wrapper around a
single command.

* Scan installed applications and see every available update at once
* Update everything, or pick individual applications
* Install from a curated catalogue of well-known Windows software
* See exactly which winget package each entry maps to
* No account, no adverts, no bundled offers

Open source under GPL-3.0. The .NET 8 runtime is bundled, so there is nothing to install first.</description>
    <summary>Free installer and updater for Windows apps, built on winget</summary>
    <releaseNotes>https://github.com/techygeekshome/AppGeek/releases/tag/v1.1.3</releaseNotes>
